{"id":"2610.28577","authors":[{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e95e","user":{"_id":"6445fd9ba56444c355dcbcba","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6445fd9ba56444c355dcbcba/NCyRCD-MK-yA0_qY6I2y0.png","isPro":false,"fullname":"Tianyu Fu","user":"fuvty","type":"user","name":"fuvty"},"name":"Tianyu Fu","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2026-10-22T08:45:05.213Z","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e95f","name":"Ruoxi Wang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e960","name":"Zihan Min","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e961","name":"Zhongqi Ren","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e962","name":"Zhihao Li","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e963","name":"Tengxuan Liu","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e964","user":{"_id":"68e7769e458298dd32cb1f6c","avatarUrl":"/avatars/267100da11dad38e8ca3971a454eb05b.svg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Shengxu Mu","user":"pinghailinfeng","type":"user","name":"pinghailinfeng"},"name":"Shengxu Mu","status":"claimed_verified","statusLastChangedAt":"2026-10-22T08:45:05.222Z","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e965","name":"Hanling Zhang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e966","name":"Yu Wang","hidden":false}],"mediaUrls":["https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/6445fd9ba56444c355dcbcba/_dP_r92LTc754Us-haved.mp4"],"publishedAt":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z","submittedOnDailyAt":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z","title":"Cache Engineering for Agents","submittedOnDailyBy":{"_id":"6445fd9ba56444c355dcbcba","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6445fd9ba56444c355dcbcba/NCyRCD-MK-yA0_qY6I2y0.png","isPro":false,"fullname":"Tianyu Fu","user":"fuvty","type":"user","name":"fuvty"},"summary":"Large Language Model (LLM) agents can handle increasingly complex tasks, navigating long trajectories of observations and actions. As these trajectories grow, key-value (KV) cache I/O and storage become the dominant cost. Trajectories can also exceed the LLM's maximum context length, requiring control over active cache growth. Prior work uses context engineering to reduce cache size by trimming or summarizing history. However, modifying the trajectory prefix invalidates subsequent cached states and triggers costly re-prefilling of retained context. Task accuracy can also suffer when too little context is retained to limit re-prefill costs. We propose cache engineering as a new scheme. It allows agents to directly control their active KV cache without modifying the trajectory or re-prefilling retained context. Specifically, agents can proactively use drop to exclude selected cache from future attention and repos to adjust retained keys' position encodings. We formalize these cache operations and identify history dependence as a serving challenge: identical token sequences can yield different cache states under different cache operation sequences, making prefix matching insufficient for correct cache reuse. Thus, we co-design the AKV serving engine. It provides a stateless interface compatible with existing serving APIs, while internally managing stateful cache reuse, eviction, and restoration. Experiments show that a tool-response rolling-drop cache policy improves average benchmark scores by 1.7 points and reduces average cost by 27.7%, compared with conventional threshold-triggered summarization. With AKV, it achieves up to 1.2x the output throughput and a 1.5x speedup in P95 request latency. Recursive self-improvement of cache policies further reduces cost by 7.1% over expert design. Our code is at https://github.com/thu-nics/AKV.","upvotes":67,"discussionId":"6ad96d683f2bb52eb8d6e967","projectPage":"https://fuvty.github.io/thinking_yard_project_page/projects/akv/","githubRepo":"https://github.com/thu-nics/AKV","githubRepoAddedBy":"user","ai_summary":"AKV introduces cache engineering to manage LLM agent key-value caches without altering trajectories, improving efficiency and accuracy via drop and repos operations with a co-designed serving engine.","ai_keywords":["key-value cache","KV cache I/O","context engineering","cache engineering","drop","repos","position encodings","history dependence","prefix matching","AKV serving engine","rolling-drop cache policy","recursive self-improvement"],"ai_summary_model":"thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small","githubStars":12,"organization":{"_id":"64b74b5fb727f8771ab887f9","name":"nics-efc","fullname":"Tsinghua-NICS-EFC","avatar":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/641031b1a78453b8d96b8420/vmgxct2WsyHcKT2x2NAYT.jpeg"},"linkedModels":[],"numTotalModels":0,"linkedDatasets":[],"numTotalDatasets":0,"linkedSpaces":[],"numTotalSpaces":0}